  :date "2026-09-02"
  :kind :expansion
  :reason
  "The two names versions 3 and 4 recorded under :absent as unwritable, now
   written. Both were refused by the same sentence -- `expression type
   mismatch: expected keyword, got i64` -- and that sentence turned out to be
   about the friendly SURFACE and not about the map: `[:map K V]` had been
   generic in its key type the whole time, and `{1 10}`, `(assoc m 1 10)`,
   `(contains? m 1)` and `(dissoc m 1)` were the four spellings that could
   not reach it (kotoba-sema ADR 0012). A second defect stood behind it and
   did not look like one: a `[:map :i64 V]` carrying TWO entries exited 70 on
   wasm32 with `internal compiler error`, because the language's own i64
   order was computed with `clojure.core/compare`, which cannot compare the
   BigInt an i64 is under nbb (kotoba-kir ADR 0257). One entry compiled and
   two did not, and `:bool`/`:string`/`:keyword` keys compiled at every entry
   count -- which is what identified it as a comparator rather than a missing
   wasm lowering.

   `get-in` ITSELF is still absent, with a new reason: in clojure.core the
   path is a value, and here it is part of the type. A one-key path answers
   the inner map and a two-key path answers an i64, so one monomorphic
   function cannot be both. `get-in2` carries the depth in its name the way
   comp2, partial1 and juxt2 carry their arity."
